WEBVTT

00:36.990 --> 00:38.836
- Hello.
- Nice to meet you.

00:38.836 --> 00:40.690
- Hi, I'm Yook Jun Seo.
- Are you free next Friday?

00:40.690 --> 00:43.053
You're Lee Ui Yeong, right?

00:44.586 --> 00:46.846
Oh my gosh!

00:48.293 --> 00:50.609
Are you okay?

00:50.609 --> 00:51.943
Aren't you hurt?

00:51.943 --> 00:53.919
- Nice to meet you.
- I'm stationed in Gyodae.

00:53.919 --> 00:55.420
I'm calling about a blind date...

00:55.420 --> 00:59.484
Every single one of these
is a blind date request?

01:00.638 --> 01:01.765
What's going on?

01:01.765 --> 01:03.792
That's what I'd like to know.

01:03.792 --> 01:05.665
Sorry?

01:06.436 --> 01:09.654
[Episode 3]

01:12.281 --> 01:13.768
Did I get hacked?

01:13.768 --> 01:14.835
Was my number leaked?

01:14.835 --> 01:15.876
My phone carrier issue?

01:15.876 --> 01:18.460
No, the shopping site?

01:19.366 --> 01:21.007
- Hello, nice to meet you.
- Who is this?

01:21.007 --> 01:23.140
This is Yoon Bak.

01:24.079 --> 01:25.563
My name is Yook Jun Seo.

01:25.563 --> 01:28.360
I'm Lee Ho Kwang, I sing and act on stage.

01:28.360 --> 01:29.946
When are you free this week?

01:29.946 --> 01:31.086
Hello, Ms. Ui Yeong.

01:31.086 --> 01:33.789
I'm Kim Do Yoon, your dermatologist's brother.

01:33.789 --> 01:34.798
What's going on?

01:34.798 --> 01:37.377
Hello, I'm Song Ji Hoon. Na Hyun's friend.

01:37.377 --> 01:39.423
I showed him your picture
and he wants to meet you.

01:39.423 --> 01:41.167
He teaches kids and he's popular.

01:41.167 --> 01:43.620
- I'll give him your number.
- Wait a second.

01:43.620 --> 01:44.892
Let me check and I'll get back to you.

01:44.892 --> 01:46.268
I gave your number to my friend.

01:46.268 --> 01:47.820
- Out of nowhere?
- I'll pass your number to him.

01:47.820 --> 01:50.520
Okay, I'll look into it.

01:56.486 --> 01:58.216
[Set me up on a blind date.]

01:59.906 --> 02:01.880
[Hey, find me a good guy.]

02:04.316 --> 02:05.442
[Paste]

02:05.442 --> 02:07.374
[Don't you have any single guy friends?]

02:07.374 --> 02:09.314
[Please set me up.]

02:11.272 --> 02:13.305
Oh my.

02:14.094 --> 02:17.379
I can't believe I did that.

02:18.258 --> 02:20.761
I'm insane!

02:24.574 --> 02:27.340
- I'm home.
- Yeah.

02:28.328 --> 02:30.819
- Oh my goodness.
- My shoulders hurt.

02:30.819 --> 02:32.313
Hey.

02:32.313 --> 02:34.199
Yeah?

02:35.232 --> 02:37.592
What is all this?

02:37.592 --> 02:41.266
You were so excited
about wearing a hotel uniform.

02:41.266 --> 02:43.672
Are you sick?

02:44.487 --> 02:46.282
- You don't have a fever...
- Come on.

02:46.282 --> 02:47.741
Mom, that's not it.

02:47.741 --> 02:49.031
From now on, when I come home drunk,

02:49.031 --> 02:51.056
turn off my phone for me.
Or just cut off my wrist.

02:51.056 --> 02:53.057
Shouldn't we cut up your credit card instead?

02:53.057 --> 02:54.598
This isn't just clothes.

02:54.598 --> 02:55.968
It's armor.

02:55.968 --> 02:57.559
Look.

02:57.559 --> 02:58.799
What kind of armor

02:58.799 --> 03:02.182
is this soft and fluffy?

03:02.182 --> 03:04.846
Then what about this?

03:04.846 --> 03:07.253
Is this camouflage cream?

03:07.253 --> 03:08.831
Oh my gosh.

03:08.831 --> 03:10.395
Don't even think about using it.

03:10.395 --> 03:13.179
Just don't touch anything else.

03:17.700 --> 03:19.510
If it hides your flaws

03:19.510 --> 03:21.290
and boosts your confidence,

03:21.290 --> 03:23.496
that's armor.

03:26.451 --> 03:28.511
Okay.

03:39.005 --> 03:41.270
It may have started as drunk texting,

03:41.270 --> 03:44.271
but an opportunity is still an opportunity.

03:47.174 --> 03:49.872
Even if it's just a one-percent chance.

03:49.872 --> 03:53.918
I just need to meet them and
find someone who's right for me.

03:55.550 --> 03:56.949
I'll look into it.

03:56.949 --> 03:59.342
Ui Yeong, I can smell the alcohol from here.

03:59.342 --> 04:00.880
- Let's grab a meal sometime.
- All of a sudden?

04:00.880 --> 04:02.413
- I'll see what I can do.
- Are you drunk?

04:02.413 --> 04:03.947
If I had someone to set you up with,
I would've dated him myself.

04:03.947 --> 04:06.452
They're just empty words...

04:06.452 --> 04:07.649
I'll look into it.

04:07.649 --> 04:09.242
But I have a favor, too.

04:09.242 --> 04:11.902
Can you book a wedding hall consultation
at your hotel for me?

04:11.902 --> 04:15.028
Yeah, it's all about give and take.

04:15.028 --> 04:16.272
Sure.

04:16.272 --> 04:19.546
So when works for you?

04:19.546 --> 04:21.349
[Hello, nice to meet you. This is Yoon Bak.]

04:21.349 --> 04:23.806
Hello, this is Lee Ui Yeong.

04:23.806 --> 04:26.706
How about this Saturday?

04:27.412 --> 04:28.843
Nice.

04:28.843 --> 04:30.336
[1:30 PM / Yoon Bak / 37]

04:30.336 --> 04:32.054
[Math Instructor]

04:32.054 --> 04:33.102
[Save]

04:33.102 --> 04:35.077
[1:30 PM / Yoon Bak / 37]

04:38.666 --> 04:41.780
Morning, Ui Yeong.

04:41.780 --> 04:44.503
Oh, is one of those for me?

04:44.503 --> 04:45.822
No, they're both mine.

04:45.822 --> 04:47.967
I need both of these to wake up.

04:47.967 --> 04:50.296
What? Didn't sleep?

04:50.296 --> 04:52.643
You look pretty, though.

04:53.256 --> 04:55.930
Why's your schedule so packed?

04:55.930 --> 04:59.719
Wait... these are blind dates?

05:01.963 --> 05:03.603
[7:30 AM / Lee Sung Jae / 31 / Designer]

05:03.603 --> 05:06.017
Who goes on a blind date before work?

05:06.017 --> 05:08.261
Yeah. That would be me.

05:08.261 --> 05:12.087
I didn't really have a choice.
I don't have time.

05:12.087 --> 05:13.817
Yesterday I was just

05:13.817 --> 05:15.917
trying to clean up the mess I made...

05:15.917 --> 05:17.447
but this isn't right, is it?

05:17.447 --> 05:19.044
It's hard enough meeting one person.

05:19.044 --> 05:20.682
And this feels kind of rude, right?

05:20.682 --> 05:21.783
Well,

05:21.783 --> 05:23.687
you're not in a relationship with any of them.

05:23.687 --> 05:25.585
As long as you give it your best each time,

05:25.585 --> 05:27.630
you've done your part.

05:27.630 --> 05:29.931
Come on, just go for it.

05:29.931 --> 05:31.251
And more importantly,

05:31.251 --> 05:33.997
if you cancel now,

05:33.997 --> 05:35.315
the blind dates will dry up.

05:35.315 --> 05:38.275
You'll lose your matchmakers for good.

05:39.795 --> 05:42.161
That can't happen.

05:47.634 --> 05:48.719
[The premium whisky brand]

05:48.719 --> 05:50.071
Starting mid-next month,

05:50.071 --> 05:52.350
our hotel will be hosting

05:52.350 --> 05:54.121
the 100th anniversary event

05:54.121 --> 05:55.809
for the premium whisky brand Deerfiddich.

05:55.809 --> 05:58.320
- Oh.
- Wow.

05:58.320 --> 06:00.382
This big project lands right
when I'm swamped...

06:00.382 --> 06:01.828
The event runs for three weeks?

06:01.828 --> 06:05.194
Yes. We're planning a whisky exhibition

06:05.194 --> 06:07.698
and tasting event as a pop-up
in the hotel lobby.

06:07.698 --> 06:08.843
The brand has entrusted us

06:08.843 --> 06:12.538
with the overall planning and operations.

06:13.812 --> 06:15.070
If that's the concept,

06:15.070 --> 06:18.616
what if we build temporary walls
and create more of a shop-in-shop feel?

06:18.616 --> 06:20.780
Put up proper signage, bring in a bartender,

06:20.780 --> 06:22.680
and recreate a whisky bar
you'd find in Scotland

06:22.680 --> 06:24.671
right in the hotel lobby.

06:24.671 --> 06:25.824
That sounds great.

06:25.824 --> 06:27.738
Let's develop it in that direction.

06:27.738 --> 06:28.811
Purchasing Team,

06:28.811 --> 06:30.980
please find a vendor that can handle
the spatial design and setup.

06:30.980 --> 06:32.370
- Got it.
- And Facilities Team,

06:32.370 --> 06:34.163
we'll need your support
during on-site construction.

06:34.163 --> 06:36.461
Say no more. We'll take care of it.

06:36.461 --> 06:39.373
So... do we get a free drink out of this?

06:54.096 --> 06:56.436
I'm counting on you.

06:58.621 --> 07:01.134
[Purchasing Team]

07:09.495 --> 07:12.426
Ui Yeong has worked nonstop this whole time.

07:12.426 --> 07:15.016
Any time there was a problem,
she showed up and fixed it. Right?

07:15.016 --> 07:16.088
Yeah.

07:16.088 --> 07:18.772
Let's let her focus on
her own life for a while.

07:18.772 --> 07:20.796
We'll put what we've learned to use.

07:20.796 --> 07:23.366
You've got to prove yourself
before your internship ends, right?

07:23.366 --> 07:26.359
Yes. I'll really give it my all.

07:26.359 --> 07:28.426
Good.

07:29.036 --> 07:31.002
- Drink up.
- Thank you.

07:32.530 --> 07:35.373
[Attorney Kang Do Hyun]
Sae Byeok, are you free tonight?

07:35.373 --> 07:37.652
- Let's talk for a minute.
- All right.

07:37.652 --> 07:39.763
Want to grab dinner
and then start looking up vendors?

07:39.763 --> 07:42.329
- Yes.
- Cheers.

07:55.119 --> 07:57.219
You look great.

08:00.550 --> 08:02.743
That looks delicious.

08:05.308 --> 08:07.215
Hello.

08:11.279 --> 08:13.470
What I realized
from going on blind dates was this.

08:13.470 --> 08:14.930
The world is big,

08:14.930 --> 08:17.030
and there are
so many different kinds of people.

08:17.030 --> 08:20.059
Not a single one was the same...

08:20.059 --> 08:22.354
not even similar.

08:22.354 --> 08:24.445
Each person was completely unique.

08:24.445 --> 08:26.822
- Each one was a universe.
- Hello, it's nice to meet you.

08:26.822 --> 08:28.032
You recognize me, right?

08:28.032 --> 08:29.302
I'm Yoon Bak.

08:29.302 --> 08:32.857
[Yoon Bak, 37, Star Math Instructor]

08:38.427 --> 08:39.831
You're done already?

08:39.831 --> 08:41.584
Would you like another soup?

08:41.584 --> 08:43.147
Already taking care of me?

08:43.147 --> 08:45.031
That's some serious flirting.

08:45.031 --> 08:46.122
Sorry?

08:46.122 --> 08:47.375
I'm kidding.

08:47.375 --> 08:49.325
I usually eat while meeting
with other instructors,

08:49.325 --> 08:51.032
so I'm used to eating fast.

08:52.588 --> 08:53.992
I see.

08:53.992 --> 08:55.443
You must be really busy.

08:55.443 --> 08:57.962
I heard your classes are extremely popular.

08:57.962 --> 08:59.986
Is that what you're really curious about?

08:59.986 --> 09:00.994
Or is it more like,

09:00.994 --> 09:02.394
"Are you too busy to date?"

09:02.394 --> 09:04.152
"Can you care about me,
not just your students?"

09:04.152 --> 09:06.172
Well...

09:07.659 --> 09:09.702
Is your schedule okay for meeting me?

09:09.702 --> 09:11.309
Time is money to me.

09:11.309 --> 09:13.499
But for you,
maybe it's silver... or even bronze.

09:13.499 --> 09:14.743
And yet here we are,

09:14.743 --> 09:16.076
focusing on each other.

09:16.076 --> 09:19.596
If these interactions keep building up,
what do you think happens?

09:20.719 --> 09:22.076
What do you think happens?

09:22.076 --> 09:23.323
Well...

09:23.323 --> 09:25.838
The ending's obvious.

09:25.838 --> 09:27.637
You've passed as my girlfriend.

09:27.637 --> 09:28.313
Sorry?

09:28.313 --> 09:30.634
If you want dating, I'll take it there.

09:30.634 --> 09:32.697
If you want marriage, I'll take it there.

09:32.697 --> 09:34.264
So don't overthink it.

09:34.264 --> 09:35.628
Just use me.

09:35.628 --> 09:36.754
It's okay.

09:36.754 --> 09:38.484
Any questions?

09:38.484 --> 09:39.674
A man who flirts

09:39.674 --> 09:41.885
like he's lecturing a room full of seniors.

09:41.885 --> 09:44.502
I heard you're really into working out.

09:44.502 --> 09:45.986
Are carbs okay?

09:45.986 --> 09:47.513
Yeah, I exercise,

09:47.513 --> 09:49.359
so I actually prefer eating a lot.

09:49.359 --> 09:51.899
[Yook Jun Seo, 29, Rehab Trainer, Former UDT]

09:53.852 --> 09:57.189
What matters most to you in a relationship?

09:57.189 --> 09:58.326
Food.

09:58.326 --> 10:00.173
If our appetites don't match,

10:00.173 --> 10:02.197
you feel that every time you eat together.

10:02.197 --> 10:04.349
What about you? Do you eat well?

10:04.349 --> 10:08.262
Yeah, I love food. I'm not picky at all.

10:08.262 --> 10:10.695
I've got tons of restaurants saved on my map.

10:10.695 --> 10:13.359
Since we're talking about it,
we could hit a few spots today.

10:13.359 --> 10:15.573
I'm getting excited already.

10:15.573 --> 10:18.306
- A few?
- Yeah.

10:21.754 --> 10:23.908
Tacos!

10:32.877 --> 10:35.079
Bagels!

10:35.079 --> 10:37.179
Gelato!

10:38.707 --> 10:40.807
Dessert!

10:47.785 --> 10:49.444
A second date with him

10:49.444 --> 10:52.657
might send my stomach into shock.

11:01.415 --> 11:04.117
Well... I was going to get the coffee today...

11:04.117 --> 11:07.490
♪ Don't say that ♪

11:07.490 --> 11:09.966
[Lee Ho Kwang, 36, Musical Actor]

11:10.628 --> 11:13.485
Today, you've given me

11:13.485 --> 11:15.806
a perfect day beyond price.

11:15.806 --> 11:18.627
From now on,

11:18.627 --> 11:21.399
you are my muse.

11:21.399 --> 11:22.510
Your... muse?

11:22.510 --> 11:24.280
Like Christine...

11:24.280 --> 11:26.313
to the Phantom.

11:26.313 --> 11:28.326
The Phantom?

11:29.013 --> 11:30.103
Mr. Ho Kwang,

11:30.103 --> 11:31.490
it's getting late,

11:31.490 --> 11:33.007
so I should head out.

11:33.007 --> 11:34.894
My place is right here. I'll go on my own.

11:34.894 --> 11:38.254
♪ No ♪

11:38.254 --> 11:41.154
I won't feel at ease unless I see you home.

11:41.154 --> 11:43.401
I can sense

11:43.401 --> 11:45.360
the dark intentions of men
circling my sunshine.

11:45.360 --> 11:47.759
The man who called me Muse, Christine,

11:47.759 --> 11:49.318
and Sunshine...

11:49.318 --> 11:50.663
and tried to overprotect me.

11:50.663 --> 11:51.942
You should probably go.

11:51.942 --> 11:54.566
Seems like she doesn't want to
share her address.

11:54.566 --> 11:55.937
Who are you, lady?

11:55.937 --> 11:58.902
Why are you interfering between us like this?

11:58.902 --> 12:00.742
Me? I'm her mother.

12:00.742 --> 12:02.473
Jesus Christ...

12:02.473 --> 12:03.979
Superstar.

12:03.979 --> 12:06.343
Not superstar. Her mother.

12:06.343 --> 12:08.169
You really don't listen, do you?

12:08.169 --> 12:09.899
And sometimes,
after meeting my greatest rival in love,

12:09.899 --> 12:11.549
things ended in total disaster.

12:11.549 --> 12:13.659
♪ Mother ♪

12:13.659 --> 12:15.103
♪ My mother... ♪

12:15.103 --> 12:18.049
♪ Your mother ♪

12:25.939 --> 12:28.550
Let us offer a prayer of gratitude
to Almighty God the Father

12:28.550 --> 12:30.794
who brought us together.

12:30.794 --> 12:32.571
[Prayer Guy, 32]
The guy who says Sunday is the Lord's Day

12:32.571 --> 12:33.974
so even dating takes the day off.

12:33.974 --> 12:35.379
Do you like drinking too?

12:35.379 --> 12:36.977
You could just drink alone at home.

12:36.977 --> 12:38.974
Why go out of your way to drink outside?

12:38.974 --> 12:40.631
[Breakup Guy, 30]
A man who clearly isn't over

12:40.631 --> 12:42.950
his ex-girlfriend yet.

12:42.950 --> 12:45.015
It's fine if we have different tastes.

12:45.015 --> 12:46.273
But what bothers me is...

12:46.273 --> 12:48.221
Why pour the sauce without even asking?

12:48.221 --> 12:50.037
I think that says a lot about you.

12:50.037 --> 12:51.828
[Sauce Guy, 35]
A dip-it guy who can't tolerate

12:51.828 --> 12:53.557
the recklessness of a pour-it-all-over girl.

12:53.557 --> 12:55.381
- Please go out with me.
- Please go out with me.

12:55.381 --> 12:56.845
- Please see me.
- Please meet me.

12:56.845 --> 12:57.944
Date me.

12:57.944 --> 13:00.770
The problem was, out of all those men,

13:00.770 --> 13:04.002
not one of them was my type.

13:20.434 --> 13:22.898
Ms. Ui Yeong!

13:22.898 --> 13:24.182
Please go out with me.

13:24.182 --> 13:26.362
Ms. Ui Yeong, wait.

13:26.362 --> 13:28.019
I love you!

13:28.019 --> 13:30.043
Stop right there!

13:30.043 --> 13:31.420
- Ms. Ui Yeong!
- Ms. Ui Yeong!

13:31.420 --> 13:33.440
Ms. Ui Yeong!

13:46.458 --> 13:48.405
When I said you passed, that meant I liked you.

13:48.405 --> 13:50.241
Let's go somewhere even better
to eat next time.

13:50.241 --> 13:53.119
Your mother has incredible charisma...

13:53.119 --> 13:54.689
[Lee Eun Mi]
We're heading to the hotel now.

13:54.689 --> 13:56.247
See you soon.

13:56.247 --> 13:58.750
Oh no, I'm late.

14:11.382 --> 14:13.308
Mr. Tae Seop.

14:17.949 --> 14:19.928
Mr. Tae Seop.

14:28.769 --> 14:30.743
Ms. Ui Yeong.

14:37.075 --> 14:39.069
You said you'd call...

14:39.069 --> 14:42.248
Don't tell me things worked out with that guy.

14:44.078 --> 14:47.044
[Director of Animal House]

14:50.610 --> 14:52.909
Hello?

14:52.909 --> 14:54.847
Hey, you're actually getting married.

14:54.847 --> 14:55.937
Congratulations.

14:55.937 --> 14:57.232
Thank you so much.

14:57.232 --> 14:59.226
It's nice having a friend who works at a hotel.

14:59.226 --> 15:00.269
It's really no big deal.

15:00.269 --> 15:03.541
Just so you know,
weekend consultations are fully booked.

15:03.541 --> 15:05.968
I'm squeezing you in as a special favor,

15:05.968 --> 15:08.534
so... don't go telling everyone, okay?

15:08.534 --> 15:09.886
Don't worry.

15:09.886 --> 15:13.931
Who else could afford a luxury hotel like this?

15:14.744 --> 15:18.005
By the way,
you two have totally different styles.

15:18.005 --> 15:19.606
We're different, but we work.

15:19.606 --> 15:22.097
Back in college,
we were on a group project together.

15:22.097 --> 15:24.939
Back then, she handled
all the work and presentations,

15:24.939 --> 15:27.919
and I just sent her 100,000 won.

15:27.919 --> 15:29.644
- And the result?
- An A-plus.

15:30.720 --> 15:34.532
There's no one who trusted me more
and delivered like you did.

15:34.532 --> 15:38.379
With all that competence,
how are you still single?

15:38.379 --> 15:39.404
- Baby.
- Yeah?

15:39.404 --> 15:40.624
Don't you have anyone

15:40.624 --> 15:43.563
you could introduce her to?

15:43.563 --> 15:44.587
You didn't even look?

15:44.587 --> 15:46.577
I told you to check.

15:46.577 --> 15:48.387
Hey, don't do that.
You're making him uncomfortable.

15:48.387 --> 15:50.288
It's fine. I'm okay.

15:50.288 --> 15:51.487
You're so clueless.

15:51.487 --> 15:52.997
Ms. Lee Eun Mi, our bride-to-be.

15:52.997 --> 15:54.804
Oh, General Manager.

15:54.804 --> 15:57.627
I'm Eun Jeong Seok,
General Manager of The Hills.

15:57.627 --> 15:58.870
Let's move to the banquet hall,

15:58.870 --> 16:00.997
where I'll introduce you
to our wedding manager.

16:00.997 --> 16:02.274
You can leave the rest to me.

16:02.274 --> 16:03.447
Please take good care of her.

16:03.447 --> 16:06.033
We'll make sure everything is perfect.

16:07.468 --> 16:09.607
I'll see you later.

16:11.154 --> 16:13.628
Ui Yeong.

16:13.628 --> 16:15.728
Why are you here?

16:17.808 --> 16:19.732
So... you were staying here,

16:19.732 --> 16:21.337
checking out,

16:21.337 --> 16:23.701
and ran into the General Manager?

16:23.701 --> 16:25.894
What if people start talking?

16:25.894 --> 16:28.687
Hey, the employee discount is sacred.

16:28.687 --> 16:29.609
And besides,

16:29.609 --> 16:32.278
if word gets around that
two consenting adults had sex,

16:32.278 --> 16:34.380
that's the ridiculous part, yeah?

16:34.380 --> 16:36.714
Beats me.

16:37.924 --> 16:38.868
But honestly,

16:38.868 --> 16:42.833
meeting people just isn't fun these days.

16:42.833 --> 16:44.630
It's always the same pattern.

16:44.630 --> 16:46.207
You meet, exchange names,

16:46.207 --> 16:47.600
eat, sleep together, and that's it.

16:47.600 --> 16:49.078
I can't see them a second time.

16:49.078 --> 16:51.524
Maybe I need a new obsession or something.

16:51.524 --> 16:54.297
I kind of see what you mean.

16:58.546 --> 17:02.145
When I said you passed, that meant I liked you.

17:03.692 --> 17:06.712
And when I said you could use me,
that was a sign of interest too.

17:06.712 --> 17:07.906
But

17:07.906 --> 17:09.190
if you keep seeing them,

17:09.190 --> 17:11.257
wouldn't feelings start to grow?

17:11.257 --> 17:14.456
They're all decent, accomplished guys.

17:14.456 --> 17:16.459
How long are you supposed to wait?

17:16.459 --> 17:18.919
Hey, if they're decent,
don't string them along.

17:18.919 --> 17:21.352
Let them find someone who's right for them.

17:21.352 --> 17:23.829
If it's not working for you, saying no is

17:23.829 --> 17:27.062
the polite thing to do in the blind date. Okay?

17:33.638 --> 17:35.055
I'm sorry.

17:35.055 --> 17:37.348
I don't think we're the right match.

17:37.348 --> 17:40.405
I hope you meet someone great.

17:45.075 --> 17:47.320
Your mother has incredible charisma.

17:47.320 --> 17:50.517
Outside your home, I could be your umbrella.

17:50.517 --> 17:52.377
Though on a sunny day like this,
you wouldn't need one.

17:52.377 --> 17:54.081
I suppose this is where our story ends.

17:54.081 --> 17:56.791
♪ The end ♪

17:56.791 --> 18:00.021
If you can end things, you can get ended too.

18:00.021 --> 18:02.981
That's just how blind dates are.

18:06.098 --> 18:07.918
You're right.

18:22.291 --> 18:24.891
- Hello.
- Hello.

18:24.891 --> 18:26.901
Hey, you've been good?

18:26.901 --> 18:29.018
Don't fight.

18:29.018 --> 18:31.104
Seoltang!

18:31.104 --> 18:32.914
Hello.

18:32.914 --> 18:35.802
Thanks for coming on such short notice.

18:35.802 --> 18:38.818
Seoltang even got a nice bath.

18:38.818 --> 18:40.239
You look so pretty.

18:40.239 --> 18:43.202
Be happy and loved in your new home,

18:43.202 --> 18:45.095
okay?

18:46.258 --> 18:48.654
Yes, thank you.

18:52.165 --> 18:55.051
[80, Geumyeonghwa 22-gil, Paju-si, Gyeonggi-do]

18:55.051 --> 18:56.935
We'd like to cancel the adoption.

18:56.935 --> 18:58.328
May I ask why?

18:58.328 --> 19:00.795
I'm sure this wasn't a snap decision.

19:00.795 --> 19:02.205
In the photos,

19:02.205 --> 19:04.122
she looked like the dog I used to have,

19:04.122 --> 19:05.455
so I felt attached.

19:05.455 --> 19:07.574
But in person, she's kind of different.

19:07.574 --> 19:09.605
Bigger than I expected.
And her fur's not that great.

19:09.605 --> 19:12.255
Was it raised outside?
It's not carrying any diseases, is it?

19:12.255 --> 19:13.925
Watch what you say.

19:13.925 --> 19:17.152
It's not like animals understand us anyway.

19:17.152 --> 19:19.915
They do.

19:19.915 --> 19:21.832
They can tell from our faces and our tone

19:21.832 --> 19:23.469
whether we're happy or upset,

19:23.469 --> 19:25.793
whether we like them or not.

19:25.793 --> 19:27.310
Someday,

19:27.310 --> 19:28.829
I hope you go through
what Seoltang went through today

19:28.829 --> 19:30.456
and feel that heartbreak yourselves.

19:30.456 --> 19:33.172
Because I don't think you'll ever understand
until you do.

19:33.172 --> 19:35.632
- What did you say?
- Let's go.

19:35.632 --> 19:36.882
Hey. Let go.

19:36.882 --> 19:38.549
What did you say?

19:38.549 --> 19:40.462
Say that again.

19:48.042 --> 19:50.265
Where are you?

19:54.862 --> 19:58.602
- Please don't run.
- Yes.

19:58.602 --> 20:00.439
He's a scammer.

20:00.439 --> 20:02.449
Wait.

20:02.449 --> 20:05.260
Mr. Song, are you okay?

20:05.260 --> 20:07.046
What's going on?

20:07.046 --> 20:08.570
You young people!

20:08.570 --> 20:10.832
A dog isn't a toy!

20:10.832 --> 20:13.429
Adopting a pet should be done carefully!

20:13.429 --> 20:14.835
And responsibly!

20:14.835 --> 20:16.409
What kind of crap is that?

20:16.409 --> 20:17.552
"Crap?"

20:17.552 --> 20:19.866
Sometimes animals are better than people.

20:19.866 --> 20:21.279
Come here, come here.

20:21.279 --> 20:23.139
Seoltang, are you okay?

20:23.139 --> 20:25.052
Who is this old guy?

20:25.052 --> 20:26.944
- What are you doing?
- Are you alright?

20:26.944 --> 20:29.449
Did you just hit me?

20:29.449 --> 20:31.238
What?

20:31.238 --> 20:34.289
I'm already pissed off.

20:34.289 --> 20:35.486
Say it again. What?

20:35.486 --> 20:38.039
So what do you want me to do?

20:53.797 --> 20:56.407
I didn't expect to be summoned
to the police station.

20:56.407 --> 20:57.966
I thought

20:57.966 --> 21:01.352
you'd handle this more like an adult.

21:06.379 --> 21:09.305
Still, our teamwork was pretty good.

21:09.305 --> 21:12.906
You look quiet, but you've got a temper.

21:12.906 --> 21:14.330
And you hold grudges.

21:14.330 --> 21:17.400
It hadn't even been five minutes,
and they were already returning her.

21:17.400 --> 21:18.477
I just lost it.

21:18.477 --> 21:20.283
Five minutes is harsh.

21:20.283 --> 21:21.943
This isn't something to brag about.

21:21.943 --> 21:24.947
I really wish people would
stop breaking records like this.

21:24.947 --> 21:26.357
I know.

21:26.357 --> 21:28.197
Oh no.

21:28.197 --> 21:29.875
You've got a dog allergy, right?

21:29.875 --> 21:31.619
I could keep her for now

21:31.619 --> 21:33.531
and take her back to the shelter this weekend.

21:33.531 --> 21:34.997
If I take my meds, I'll be fine for a few days.

21:34.997 --> 21:36.145
I'll keep her.

21:36.145 --> 21:37.605
Alright then.

21:37.605 --> 21:39.597
Seoltang,

21:39.597 --> 21:43.177
maybe you're headed somewhere better, huh?

21:47.343 --> 21:48.829
That's my phone.

21:53.898 --> 21:56.442
Sir, I heard my friend made a reservation.

21:56.442 --> 21:57.915
You even came in on your day off.

21:57.915 --> 22:00.093
That's another brownie point for you. Thanks.

22:00.093 --> 22:02.679
You're welcome.

22:03.631 --> 22:05.230
You're waiting on a call?

22:05.230 --> 22:08.016
Yes. From Ms. Ui Yeong.

22:14.047 --> 22:16.997
Well, as the matchmaker,
I do have some responsibility.

22:16.997 --> 22:19.604
I should probably tell you this
in good conscience.

22:19.604 --> 22:21.107
About Ms. Ui Yeong...

22:21.107 --> 22:22.864
I know she's going on other blind dates.

22:22.864 --> 22:24.873
I saw her with another guy.

22:25.507 --> 22:27.192
You even saw?

22:27.192 --> 22:29.527
And you're still waiting?

22:29.527 --> 22:32.331
Well... she said she'd call.

22:32.331 --> 22:34.355
And it's not over between us.

22:34.355 --> 22:36.720
Is that confidence?

22:36.720 --> 22:39.095
Or are you just clueless?

22:39.682 --> 22:41.619
If I see her one more time,

22:41.619 --> 22:44.532
I think I'll know for sure.

22:46.856 --> 22:48.701
Oh, man.

22:48.701 --> 22:50.255
Well...

22:50.255 --> 22:52.272
A matchmaker's just a matchmaker.

22:52.272 --> 22:54.692
Not Cupid.

22:57.310 --> 22:59.231
Then...

22:59.231 --> 23:01.927
Run into her one more time.

23:01.927 --> 23:03.528
Sorry?

23:03.528 --> 23:04.545
What do you mean?

23:04.545 --> 23:07.542
Think of it as warranty service.

23:07.542 --> 23:09.702
That's how hotels work, right?

23:09.702 --> 23:11.399
For some, it's a workplace.

23:11.399 --> 23:14.738
A place they have to stay eight hours a day.

23:14.738 --> 23:17.589
For others, it's somewhere
you drop by for a meeting

23:17.589 --> 23:21.002
or a cup of coffee with a friend.

23:21.002 --> 23:24.815
So... just happen to run into her
one more time.

23:30.182 --> 23:31.993
Ms. Ui Yeong.

23:31.993 --> 23:34.355
This is the hotel you work at...

23:37.885 --> 23:41.452
I'm just here to meet a friend.

23:44.059 --> 23:46.702
Since we ran into each other like this,

23:46.702 --> 23:50.182
want to grab a bite together?

23:50.182 --> 23:53.242
Why am I holding her hand?

23:54.242 --> 23:56.635
Ms. Ui Yeong?

23:56.635 --> 23:57.979
Ms. Ui Yeong.

23:57.979 --> 23:59.962
Ms. Ui Yeong?

23:59.962 --> 24:02.935
Ms. Seoltang...

24:02.935 --> 24:05.440
What do I do?

24:05.440 --> 24:06.109
[Purchasing Team Conference Room]

24:06.109 --> 24:07.191
HOME is a brand

24:07.191 --> 24:09.373
that's been getting a lot of buzz lately

24:09.373 --> 24:11.584
among people into home styling.

24:11.584 --> 24:13.454
[Vendor Portfolios]

24:13.454 --> 24:16.698
They've also done cafe remodels like this.

24:16.698 --> 24:18.722
We're not playing house.

24:18.722 --> 24:20.204
We've worked with Homage plenty.

24:20.204 --> 24:21.923
Let's just go with them.

24:21.923 --> 24:24.873
Of course Homage is great,
but this looks impressive too.

24:24.873 --> 24:26.930
Why don't we get proposals from both

24:26.930 --> 24:28.903
and decide after reviewing them?

24:28.903 --> 24:30.707
That's more work for us.

24:30.707 --> 24:32.404
Do we really need to go that far?

24:32.404 --> 24:35.244
Making sure the space turns out right
is part of our job too.

24:35.244 --> 24:36.627
Let's request a proposal.

24:36.627 --> 24:38.354
Should we give them about two weeks?

24:38.354 --> 24:40.585
Even a rough draft is fine. Make it one week.

24:40.585 --> 24:42.467
One week might be...

24:42.467 --> 24:44.132
a bit tight.

24:44.132 --> 24:46.483
Then let's make it ten days.

24:46.483 --> 24:48.656
If you're going to decide
everything yourselves,

24:48.656 --> 24:50.402
why even ask me?

24:50.402 --> 24:51.852
I'll contact Homage.

24:51.852 --> 24:53.790
You handle the rest.

24:53.790 --> 24:55.656
Okay. I'll reach out to HOME.

24:55.656 --> 24:57.318
Oh, right. Sae Byeok.

24:57.318 --> 24:58.975
Since she found the vendor,

24:58.975 --> 25:00.669
why don't we let her handle the contact?

25:00.669 --> 25:02.247
I'll send the email,

25:02.247 --> 25:05.182
and she can take care of
the detailed communication.

25:05.831 --> 25:07.704
Want to give it a try?

25:07.704 --> 25:11.302
Yes. I'll do it.

25:11.302 --> 25:14.292
[The Hills & Deerfiddich Whisky Brand Pop-up]
[Designated Bid Proposal]

25:14.292 --> 25:16.036
[Your email has been sent successfully.]
Done.

25:16.036 --> 25:17.102
- Sae Byeok.
- Yeah.

25:17.102 --> 25:18.137
Now that the email's sent,

25:18.137 --> 25:20.266
give them a call and let's head out.

25:20.266 --> 25:21.296
Okay.

25:21.296 --> 25:23.174
- Great work today.
- Good work.

25:23.174 --> 25:25.936
- You head home early too.
- Yes.

25:38.806 --> 25:40.910
Hello, this is Lee Eun Ho from HOME.

25:40.910 --> 25:42.116
Hello,

25:42.116 --> 25:44.986
this is Sim Sae Byeok
from the Purchasing Team at The Hills.

25:44.986 --> 25:48.546
I just sent you an email.

25:49.633 --> 25:51.595
I see.

25:51.595 --> 25:54.211
- About the pop-up?
- Yes, that's right.

25:54.211 --> 25:56.959
[Ms. Hyun Min, HOME checked the email
and will get back to us.]

26:04.843 --> 26:06.809
- Isn't she that intern?
- Who?

26:06.809 --> 26:08.633
You know, Do Hyun's...

26:08.633 --> 26:11.353
- Oh, that intern.
- Yeah.

26:12.359 --> 26:14.757
Interns these days really know
how to make work interesting.

26:14.757 --> 26:17.243
Tell me about it.

26:27.370 --> 26:28.934
Attorney Kang,

26:28.934 --> 26:32.267
may I speak with you for a moment?

26:36.795 --> 26:39.468
No, stay seated.

26:42.101 --> 26:43.798
Enjoy your drink.

26:43.798 --> 26:46.207
Thank you.

26:56.533 --> 26:59.574
So... have you given it some thought?

26:59.574 --> 27:01.587
Yes.

27:02.494 --> 27:06.591
I feel uneasy about Ms. Ui Yeong,

27:06.591 --> 27:10.764
and right now,
getting a job is my top priority.

27:10.764 --> 27:13.191
I'm sorry.

27:16.044 --> 27:19.181
I've been rejected like this before.

27:19.181 --> 27:22.708
Back then, I had nothing to offer,
so I just backed off.

27:22.708 --> 27:24.331
But things are different now.

27:24.331 --> 27:26.158
I can buy you meals,

27:26.158 --> 27:28.636
I can support you with
what you need for employment.

27:28.636 --> 27:30.688
You should think about
what would benefit you more...

27:30.688 --> 27:32.235
To be honest,

27:32.235 --> 27:33.828
it's actually put me at a disadvantage.

27:33.828 --> 27:35.925
I haven't even had the chance to prove myself,

27:35.925 --> 27:37.985
but people at the company already recognize me

27:37.985 --> 27:40.497
because you said you liked me.

27:40.497 --> 27:42.221
The project I'm handling this time...

27:42.221 --> 27:44.685
I'm going to give it everything I've got.

27:44.685 --> 27:48.091
Please help me focus on my work.

27:49.218 --> 27:52.731
I'll get going now.

28:16.585 --> 28:18.516
Do you need more support frames for the legs?

28:18.516 --> 28:19.547
[The Hills & Deerfiddich Whisky Brand Pop-up]

28:19.547 --> 28:21.287
We'll simplify the frame
and use straps instead.

28:21.287 --> 28:23.229
[We would like to propose your company
as a designated bidder.]

28:23.229 --> 28:25.866
Hey, Lee Eun Ho. Did you see the email?

28:25.866 --> 28:27.270
- Which one?
- The Hills pop-up.

28:27.270 --> 28:28.528
Yeah, I saw it.

28:28.528 --> 28:29.821
But I was going to turn it down.

28:29.821 --> 28:31.255
Our schedule's already tight,

28:31.255 --> 28:32.508
and you hate pop-ups anyway.

28:32.508 --> 28:33.832
All that work for something temporary.

28:33.832 --> 28:36.799
Yeah, I do hate them.

28:36.799 --> 28:39.410
But we're doing this one.

28:39.410 --> 28:40.434
Doing what?

28:40.434 --> 28:42.149
You don't have to.
We've got plenty to do already.

28:42.149 --> 28:43.528
No.

28:43.528 --> 28:45.754
- I want to do it.
- What?

28:45.754 --> 28:46.998
Where are you going?

28:46.998 --> 28:48.685
The hotel. To check out the space.

28:48.685 --> 28:50.195
Right now?

28:50.195 --> 28:52.089
You're really doing this?

28:52.089 --> 28:53.199
Yeah.

28:53.199 --> 28:56.959
I was planning to go today anyway.

28:56.959 --> 28:58.396
Ms. Ui Yeong.

28:58.396 --> 28:59.582
Yes?

28:59.582 --> 29:02.799
I heard back from Lee Eun Ho at HOME.

29:02.799 --> 29:04.419
He said they want to participate in the bid.

29:04.419 --> 29:06.509
Really? That's great.

29:06.509 --> 29:10.173
I felt bad dumping all the work
on you and Hyun Min.

29:10.173 --> 29:13.153
I'll treat you both properly next time.

29:27.401 --> 29:29.860
So this is the place.

29:34.351 --> 29:36.851
I'm so sorry. Are you okay?

29:36.851 --> 29:39.100
I'm okay, thanks.

29:49.442 --> 29:51.788
I'll see her again... right?

29:55.666 --> 29:57.530
I need to take this call. Go on ahead.

29:57.530 --> 29:59.400
Okay.

30:01.385 --> 30:02.409
Hello?

30:02.409 --> 30:04.042
Is this Ms. Lee Ui Yeong's phone?

30:04.042 --> 30:05.592
I got your number from Ms. Eun Mi.

30:05.592 --> 30:07.012
This is Kim Su On.

30:07.012 --> 30:08.902
Oh, yeah.

30:08.902 --> 30:10.309
Hello.

30:10.309 --> 30:12.459
Sorry for calling out of the blue.

30:12.459 --> 30:15.719
Are you free tomorrow evening?

30:19.487 --> 30:21.363
I heard a lot about you from Ms. Eun Mi.

30:21.363 --> 30:23.166
She kept saying how nice you are.

30:23.166 --> 30:25.549
I wasn't expecting much looks-wise...

30:26.879 --> 30:29.303
You're very beautiful.

30:29.303 --> 30:32.127
[Kim Su On, 35, Family Business Owner]

30:32.127 --> 30:35.167
Thank you.

30:35.167 --> 30:36.517
I heard

30:36.517 --> 30:39.017
you and Mr. Ho Jin
have been friends for a long time.

30:39.017 --> 30:40.984
Yeah, that punk...

30:40.984 --> 30:43.574
It's been about twenty years already
with that guy.

30:43.574 --> 30:44.746
We should go on

30:44.746 --> 30:46.418
a double date sometime, the four of us.

30:46.418 --> 30:48.341
Right?

30:53.463 --> 30:56.516
So what are your parents' hobbies?

30:56.516 --> 30:58.947
My parents' hobbies?

30:58.947 --> 31:00.849
Yes.

31:01.829 --> 31:05.793
My mom has been doing yoga for a long time,

31:05.793 --> 31:10.283
and my dad used to enjoy fishing and camping,

31:10.283 --> 31:11.729
but these days he doesn't really...

31:11.729 --> 31:15.109
I heard your father works for the railway.

31:16.046 --> 31:17.830
Yes, that's right.

31:17.830 --> 31:21.153
And that you live separately
because of his job.

31:22.404 --> 31:25.358
Well, not just because of his job.

31:25.358 --> 31:28.828
It's my parents' situation,
so I don't know everything,

31:28.828 --> 31:32.791
but they've lived apart since I was young

31:32.791 --> 31:35.298
because their personalities
and values are very different.

31:37.518 --> 31:39.275
So are they divorced?

31:39.275 --> 31:40.922
No, not divorced.

31:40.922 --> 31:43.582
- Separated.
- I see.

31:43.582 --> 31:46.229
Well, that's a relief.

31:46.229 --> 31:47.254
"A relief?"

31:47.254 --> 31:49.832
You seem like someone who grew up very loved.

31:49.832 --> 31:53.112
Honestly, I never would've guessed
if you hadn't told me.

32:10.290 --> 32:12.643
So tired.

32:22.332 --> 32:23.910
Oh, Eun Mi.

32:23.910 --> 32:25.551
Hey, I heard you met Su On today.

32:25.551 --> 32:28.430
How was he? Isn't he kind of interesting?

32:29.356 --> 32:31.960
He sure knows how to say
boring things with confidence.

32:31.960 --> 32:34.067
He's just honest.

32:34.067 --> 32:35.431
You know what he told me?

32:35.431 --> 32:38.364
He usually likes girls from happy families,

32:38.364 --> 32:40.817
but he wants to see you again.

32:43.498 --> 32:45.088
What does that even mean?

32:45.088 --> 32:48.001
I heard your parents are living separately.

32:48.001 --> 32:50.598
Why didn't you tell me?

32:50.598 --> 32:52.558
I never hid it.

32:52.558 --> 32:54.782
You don't have to share everything
to be friends.

32:54.782 --> 32:55.902
The point is,

32:55.902 --> 32:57.012
he wants a second date.

32:57.012 --> 32:58.859
That means it went well.

32:58.859 --> 33:00.277
Oh, and he's wondering

33:00.277 --> 33:03.032
if your parents are financially prepared
for retirement.

33:03.032 --> 33:04.866
What?

33:04.866 --> 33:06.436
Why would he want to know that?

33:06.436 --> 33:08.460
Well, it's good for you to know too.

33:08.460 --> 33:09.906
It doesn't have to be detailed.

33:09.906 --> 33:12.579
Just a simple yes or no.

33:13.325 --> 33:15.501
He's asking way too much.

33:15.501 --> 33:17.697
I'm hanging up.

34:28.270 --> 34:30.440
[Dad]

34:33.937 --> 34:35.694
I can't just call my dad

34:35.694 --> 34:38.307
and ask about retirement.

34:43.550 --> 34:45.923
Mom?

34:45.923 --> 34:46.994
What are you doing?

34:46.994 --> 34:48.973
Nothing.

34:50.517 --> 34:52.387
Don't stay up too late on your phone.

34:52.387 --> 34:54.447
I'm not a high schooler anymore.

34:54.447 --> 34:56.273
Good night.

35:03.984 --> 35:06.317
Yeah, this really isn't right.

35:06.317 --> 35:07.647
My parents' retirement?

35:07.647 --> 35:10.930
I dated just fine
without knowing stuff like that.

35:14.809 --> 35:18.481
I don't think Mr. Su On and I are a good match.

35:18.481 --> 35:21.281
Tell him for me, okay?

35:26.447 --> 35:28.407
Alright.

35:29.790 --> 35:31.789
What's this?

35:32.650 --> 35:34.807
I still have something with the tag on.

35:34.807 --> 35:37.493
Nice. I can return it.

35:39.745 --> 35:42.078
Oh my, that's a lot.

35:42.078 --> 35:43.736
- By this week.
- What?

35:43.736 --> 35:46.017
Get it done by the end of the week.

36:13.184 --> 36:15.634
We said we'd get proposals
from the vendors, right?

36:15.634 --> 36:17.604
Let's just review Homage and be done with it.

36:17.604 --> 36:19.218
Sorry? Why?

36:19.218 --> 36:21.922
It's a waste of time.
When would we review all that?

36:21.922 --> 36:24.133
Honestly, we were going with Homage anyway.

36:24.133 --> 36:27.176
They just did that to give you the job.

36:27.176 --> 36:29.140
Let's not make things complicated.

36:29.140 --> 36:32.850
Then I'll just check with Ms. Ui Yeong first...

36:32.850 --> 36:34.874
You're saying you need Ui Yeong's approval

36:34.874 --> 36:38.040
for what I just said?

36:38.040 --> 36:40.860
No, that's not what I meant.

36:40.860 --> 36:43.160
Sorry.

36:44.552 --> 36:45.962
- Ms. Sae Byeok.
- Yes.

36:45.962 --> 36:48.972
Handling situations like this
is part of the job.

36:48.972 --> 36:53.189
I'll make sure this proposal
turns out perfect on my side.

36:53.189 --> 36:55.990
Just wrap things up cleanly
so the other vendor doesn't make a fuss.

36:55.990 --> 36:58.452
Yes, understood.

37:08.386 --> 37:11.499
[Conference Room]
Hello.

37:11.499 --> 37:13.116
I'm Oh Man Joong, CEO of Homage.

37:13.116 --> 37:16.769
Even your business card looks impressive.

37:20.205 --> 37:22.269
We successfully wrapped up the exhibition

37:22.269 --> 37:23.809
at Place Hotel earlier this year,

37:23.809 --> 37:26.488
and what was the other one... last week?

37:26.488 --> 37:27.636
Oh right,

37:27.636 --> 37:29.413
the Bella Museum.

37:29.413 --> 37:30.906
As we mentioned in the email,

37:30.906 --> 37:33.669
our exhibition will focus on objects.

37:33.669 --> 37:35.566
So we just need to build some showcases.

37:35.566 --> 37:37.837
Let me show you the jewelry store opening

37:37.837 --> 37:40.003
we did at New World Department Store in 2017.

37:40.003 --> 37:41.923
Yes.

37:48.979 --> 37:51.512
Here it is.

37:53.589 --> 37:55.399
Next is the delivery schedule.

37:55.399 --> 37:56.923
Construction needs to be completed at least...

37:56.923 --> 37:58.116
Miss?

37:58.116 --> 37:59.476
We're not some small-time shop.

37:59.476 --> 38:01.706
We've done pop-ups like this in our sleep.

38:01.706 --> 38:03.735
You think a company that collaborates with

38:03.735 --> 38:05.203
city halls and department stores

38:05.203 --> 38:07.067
can't meet a deadline?

38:07.067 --> 38:08.358
Of course, but

38:08.358 --> 38:09.699
we just need to confirm the process...

38:09.699 --> 38:11.849
Ms. Sara, show them the proposal.

38:11.849 --> 38:13.755
Yes.

38:16.489 --> 38:19.268
Oh wow, already?

38:21.995 --> 38:23.968
Wow.

38:27.293 --> 38:28.885
You prepared something this detailed

38:28.885 --> 38:31.043
in such a short time?

38:31.043 --> 38:33.513
We'll use lauan plywood

38:33.513 --> 38:36.057
to bring out the vintage mood of a whisky bar.

38:36.057 --> 38:38.774
Some of the wood surfaces
will be finished with Formica

38:38.774 --> 38:42.260
to highlight Deerfiddich's signature color.

38:42.260 --> 38:44.870
Such high quality in so little time.

38:44.870 --> 38:47.658
Professionals really are different.

38:47.658 --> 38:50.484
What do you think, Manager?

38:50.484 --> 38:52.797
Looks good.

38:58.306 --> 39:01.106
It looks so classy.

39:01.106 --> 39:02.781
- Thank you for your time.
- Thank you.

39:02.781 --> 39:04.954
- Thank you for coming.
- This way, please.

39:04.954 --> 39:07.591
Thank you so much, Mr. Oh.

39:07.591 --> 39:09.801
And you look very stylish today too.

39:09.801 --> 39:10.886
You're too kind.

39:10.886 --> 39:12.496
If your schedule allows,

39:12.496 --> 39:15.962
maybe we could grab a drink.

39:19.065 --> 39:20.541
Hey, Sae Byeok.

39:20.541 --> 39:25.668
Have you scheduled the meeting
with the CEO of HOME yet?

39:25.668 --> 39:28.092
Actually... you know...

39:28.092 --> 39:31.285
I heard back from him...

39:32.119 --> 39:34.368
but...

39:34.368 --> 39:36.672
due to internal reasons,

39:36.672 --> 39:39.671
there's been a change of plans,

39:40.359 --> 39:41.842
and they said they have to drop out.

39:41.842 --> 39:43.156
Drop out?

39:43.156 --> 39:47.202
After the project's already underway?

39:51.150 --> 39:53.854
So that's why you looked down earlier.

39:53.854 --> 39:56.511
You worked hard on this.
That must be disappointing.

39:56.511 --> 39:59.308
It's okay. This happens sometimes.

39:59.308 --> 40:00.615
Yeah.

40:00.615 --> 40:01.732
Still,

40:01.732 --> 40:04.296
I'm just glad we get to work with

40:04.296 --> 40:07.185
such capable people.

40:07.185 --> 40:08.702
Yeah, don't worry.

40:08.702 --> 40:10.602
Okay.

40:14.778 --> 40:17.578
- Let's wrap up.
- Okay.

40:27.673 --> 40:30.800
Is this exhibition flow too complicated?

40:30.800 --> 40:32.470
Oh, I like it.

40:32.470 --> 40:34.066
Yeah.

40:34.066 --> 40:36.586
Looks great, but...

40:37.287 --> 40:39.707
we're out.

40:39.707 --> 40:41.740
What?

40:41.740 --> 40:44.913
We haven't even had the meeting yet.

40:45.820 --> 40:47.550
Got a cigarette?

40:47.550 --> 40:49.703
I quit a long time ago.

40:50.633 --> 40:53.728
It pisses me off that
they just canceled over "internal reasons."

40:53.728 --> 40:56.880
Usually they at least say
the budget didn't work out.

40:56.880 --> 40:58.904
This is just plain disrespectful.

40:58.904 --> 41:01.637
They probably already had a vendor lined up.

41:01.637 --> 41:04.607
That excuse is way too obvious.

41:04.607 --> 41:06.111
If that's really the case,

41:06.111 --> 41:10.093
maybe it's better things ended now.

41:10.093 --> 41:13.447
You stayed up for days
trying to match their plans, didn't you?

41:13.447 --> 41:16.240
Want to get some air?

41:16.240 --> 41:19.893
Yeah. Let's take Sua out for a bit.

41:26.384 --> 41:28.950
- Good work today.
- Thank you.

41:29.942 --> 41:31.319
Hello?

41:31.319 --> 41:33.639
Guess you didn't save my number.

41:33.639 --> 41:35.743
This is Su On.

41:35.743 --> 41:38.900
I asked Ms. Eun Mi to tell you
I wanted to see you again.

41:38.900 --> 41:41.711
Did Eun Mi not pass along what I said?

41:41.711 --> 41:43.362
Are you free after work?

41:43.362 --> 41:44.664
I've got something to take care of.

41:44.664 --> 41:46.807
I happen to be near your hotel.

41:46.807 --> 41:49.508
Oh, really?

41:49.508 --> 41:52.428
Yes, I'm available.

41:53.541 --> 41:55.401
Okay.

42:04.954 --> 42:08.734
I actually brought this to return...

42:17.151 --> 42:18.402
Ms. Ui Yeong.

42:18.402 --> 42:21.758
That outfit looks really good on you today.

42:21.758 --> 42:25.265
Pink's not easy to pull off.

42:25.265 --> 42:27.578
Thank you.

42:27.578 --> 42:29.695
Mr. Su On,

42:29.695 --> 42:33.788
I heard you were asking
about my parents' retirement plans.

42:33.788 --> 42:34.812
Yes.

42:34.812 --> 42:37.148
Why?

42:37.148 --> 42:38.745
Well... this is just my opinion, but

42:38.745 --> 42:42.032
we're not meeting with marriage
in mind right now,

42:42.032 --> 42:43.562
and my parents' retirement

42:43.562 --> 42:46.449
is something for me
and my parents to figure out.

42:46.449 --> 42:50.869
It's not something you need to plan for.

42:50.869 --> 42:52.856
Oh, I see.

42:52.856 --> 42:54.643
That's fair.

42:54.643 --> 42:57.456
Don't worry about it.

42:59.743 --> 43:01.488
Let's change the mood a bit.

43:01.488 --> 43:03.267
How about a bottle of wine?

43:03.267 --> 43:05.447
Okay.

43:05.447 --> 43:08.247
- Excuse me.
- Yes?

43:10.920 --> 43:14.480
Can we have a cheese platter
and a bottle of wine?

43:15.695 --> 43:17.628
This one, please.

43:17.628 --> 43:21.121
- Lee Jeong Woo?
- I'll bring that right out.

43:36.987 --> 43:38.859
[Shin Ji Su]

43:38.859 --> 43:40.209
Oh right...

43:40.209 --> 43:43.962
If it's Lee Jeong Woo,
he should have a tattoo on his neck.

43:59.856 --> 44:01.880
I heard you can drink pretty well.

44:01.880 --> 44:04.707
What's your actual limit?

44:04.707 --> 44:06.558
Well, it depends on what I'm drinking.

44:06.558 --> 44:07.891
For wine... maybe a bottle?

44:07.891 --> 44:09.868
That's way more than me.

44:09.868 --> 44:12.903
I guess I'll have to pour you a bit more
to keep up with you.

44:12.903 --> 44:14.599
Yeah.

44:14.599 --> 44:15.911
Excuse me,

44:15.911 --> 44:18.000
I need to use the restroom.

44:18.000 --> 44:20.139
Sure.

44:26.825 --> 44:29.078
Excuse me.

44:30.292 --> 44:34.185
This might be an odd question, but...

44:34.185 --> 44:37.472
are you by any chance a twin?

44:37.472 --> 44:39.719
No, I'm an only child.

44:39.719 --> 44:43.172
Oh... sorry about that.

44:44.046 --> 44:46.069
If it were twins,

44:46.069 --> 44:48.743
wouldn't the last names match?

44:48.743 --> 44:50.016
Huh?

44:50.016 --> 44:51.660
I'm Shin,

44:51.660 --> 44:54.173
and the person you know is Lee.

44:54.173 --> 44:56.872
Right, that's true.

44:58.559 --> 45:00.520
It is you, isn't it?

45:00.520 --> 45:01.985
Lee Jeong Woo.

45:01.985 --> 45:03.282
What are you doing here?

45:03.282 --> 45:04.521
Isn't it obvious?

45:04.521 --> 45:08.016
- I'm working part-time.
- I mean why are you here?

45:08.016 --> 45:10.323
Another blind date?

45:10.323 --> 45:12.622
You really want a relationship, huh?

45:12.622 --> 45:13.372
What?

45:13.372 --> 45:17.462
You kept going on about dating last time too.

45:19.003 --> 45:20.853
The guy's not bad.

45:20.853 --> 45:23.925
He's got eyes, a nose, a mouth.

45:23.925 --> 45:25.926
He dresses well too.

45:25.926 --> 45:27.906
Just your type.

45:27.906 --> 45:29.290
And what exactly is my type?

45:29.290 --> 45:30.676
Good luck.

45:30.676 --> 45:34.263
But if you end up not liking him,

45:34.263 --> 45:36.509
just do this.

45:36.509 --> 45:38.896
Like this. Send me a signal.

45:38.896 --> 45:40.469
Okay?

45:40.469 --> 45:42.402
Hey...

45:46.275 --> 45:49.347
What is wrong with him?

46:04.702 --> 46:06.028
Well...

46:06.028 --> 46:07.313
Mr. Su On,

46:07.313 --> 46:11.686
I think we should move somewhere
more comfortable.

46:13.068 --> 46:14.318
Oh, okay.

46:14.318 --> 46:15.844
Do you have somewhere in mind?

46:15.844 --> 46:18.065
No place in particular.

46:18.065 --> 46:19.463
Anywhere's fine.

46:19.463 --> 46:20.867
Just not here.

46:20.867 --> 46:24.235
Anywhere is fine?

46:24.235 --> 46:25.465
Sounds good.

46:25.465 --> 46:27.310
Let me use the restroom first.

46:27.310 --> 46:29.410
Sure.

46:41.230 --> 46:43.254
What is wrong with him...

46:43.254 --> 46:45.167
Ms. Eun Mi told me

46:45.167 --> 46:48.073
she turned down the second date.

46:49.127 --> 46:52.457
She's nothing special, and she turns me down?

46:52.457 --> 46:54.867
I just called her out because I was bored.

46:54.867 --> 46:57.500
You know what really killed the mood?

46:57.500 --> 47:00.565
She came out with the tag still on her clothes.

47:00.565 --> 47:02.935
If I take the tag off for her,

47:02.935 --> 47:05.508
does that make her mine?

47:06.207 --> 47:08.474
Beats me.

47:09.560 --> 47:11.787
Yeah.

47:11.787 --> 47:14.793
She wants to move somewhere more comfortable.

47:14.793 --> 47:18.172
Where should we go? A nice motel?

47:19.220 --> 47:21.356
It's slippery.

47:21.356 --> 47:24.322
Sorry about that.

47:27.131 --> 47:29.105
What?

47:30.298 --> 47:34.171
There's no water here...

47:37.419 --> 47:38.729
Let's go.

47:38.729 --> 47:40.576
- What are you doing?
- I'll explain outside.

47:40.576 --> 47:43.040
- Hey, let go.
- What's going on?

47:43.040 --> 47:44.860
Mr. Su On, it's just...

47:44.860 --> 47:46.390
Ui Yeong,

47:46.390 --> 47:49.004
looks like your taste in men has changed.

47:49.004 --> 47:50.297
You...

47:50.297 --> 47:52.320
You shoved me on purpose
in the restroom, didn't you?

47:52.320 --> 47:53.824
Do you know him?

47:53.824 --> 47:55.858
No, I don't know him. Let's just go.

47:55.858 --> 47:58.063
You're really leaving?

47:58.063 --> 48:00.589
- I know how you feel.
- What?

48:00.589 --> 48:03.341
You came because
you wanted to see me, didn't you?

48:03.341 --> 48:04.757
What's wrong with you?

48:04.757 --> 48:07.258
I couldn't sleep or eat because I missed you.

48:07.258 --> 48:09.749
Look at me. Don't I look thinner?

48:09.749 --> 48:10.800
Hey.

48:12.484 --> 48:14.235
So you were using me.

48:14.235 --> 48:15.137
What?

48:15.137 --> 48:17.551
Unbelievable.

48:17.551 --> 48:19.348
You act all classy,

48:19.348 --> 48:21.176
but your situation with men is a mess.

48:21.176 --> 48:22.979
Who's the real mess here?

48:22.979 --> 48:23.938
You hit me?

48:23.938 --> 48:25.405
Hey, stop!

48:25.405 --> 48:26.929
- Stop it!
- Darn it.

48:26.929 --> 48:29.276
Stop...

48:29.276 --> 48:31.426
- Are you...
- What's going on?

48:31.426 --> 48:33.585
Are you okay?

48:33.585 --> 48:36.771
You pushed me first.

48:38.058 --> 48:40.245
Oh gosh.

48:41.225 --> 48:43.965
I'm sorry.

48:56.487 --> 48:58.893
I'll take you home.

48:58.893 --> 49:01.760
Why would you take me home?

49:01.760 --> 49:03.980
You had wine.

49:03.980 --> 49:06.264
First you interfere,
then you act like you care.

49:06.264 --> 49:08.015
Make up your mind.

49:08.015 --> 49:10.108
Is there some reason for this?

49:10.108 --> 49:13.364
Tell me so I can understand.

49:13.364 --> 49:15.597
Well...

49:16.871 --> 49:18.788
You tucked your hair behind your ear.

49:18.788 --> 49:20.246
I thought it was a signal.

49:20.246 --> 49:22.874
That you wanted me to rescue you.

49:26.811 --> 49:28.885
Do I look that pathetic to you?

49:28.885 --> 49:30.379
"Why does she live like this?"

49:30.379 --> 49:32.298
"Why is she so desperate for love?"
That's what you think, isn't it?

49:32.298 --> 49:33.826
That's not it.

49:33.826 --> 49:35.003
But you know what?

49:35.003 --> 49:36.723
You're even more ridiculous.

49:36.723 --> 49:40.029
So funny I can't even laugh.

49:41.372 --> 49:43.423
You're fake.

49:43.423 --> 49:46.757
The blind date was fake, your name was fake.

49:46.757 --> 49:48.873
And someone like you thinks I'm ridiculous...

49:48.873 --> 49:51.773
Why wouldn't I find you ridiculous?

50:37.801 --> 50:39.886
How long are you going to keep following me?

50:39.886 --> 50:42.598
Until you calm down.

50:42.598 --> 50:45.257
What's with him?

50:45.257 --> 50:47.897
Just go now.

50:53.545 --> 50:54.736
[The Seagull]

50:54.736 --> 50:56.291
Here.

50:56.291 --> 50:58.165
What is this?

50:58.165 --> 51:01.497
My name's not Lee Jeong Woo. It's Shin Ji Su.

51:01.497 --> 51:03.342
I'm an actor.

51:03.342 --> 51:06.125
I'm twenty-nine.

51:06.125 --> 51:08.722
I went on that blind date for someone else
because of a situation.

51:08.722 --> 51:11.555
And the reason is...

51:12.327 --> 51:15.113
I can't tell you.

51:15.113 --> 51:17.189
I'm not curious about your story.

51:17.189 --> 51:20.355
Even if I knew, it wouldn't change anything.

51:22.004 --> 51:24.254
Just take it.

51:24.254 --> 51:26.348
It's basically my ID.

51:26.348 --> 51:30.294
I just didn't want to be
completely fake with you.

51:34.737 --> 51:36.974
I don't understand you.

51:36.974 --> 51:40.507
I don't get why you want love that badly.

51:40.507 --> 51:41.712
But

51:41.712 --> 51:44.920
I've never once looked down on you.

51:49.582 --> 51:52.146
Okay. Just go.

51:52.146 --> 51:54.484
Wait.

52:14.801 --> 52:16.139
What?

52:16.139 --> 52:17.642
What did you just do?

52:17.642 --> 52:19.155
Well...

52:19.155 --> 52:22.761
You had something on your back.

52:26.733 --> 52:29.599
Please come see the play.

52:30.446 --> 52:33.146
I'll get going then.

53:22.935 --> 53:24.038
- Yeah.
- Hey.

53:24.038 --> 53:26.702
Why haven't you been answering?

53:26.702 --> 53:29.095
Are you outside?

53:31.042 --> 53:32.893
Are you okay?

53:32.893 --> 53:34.170
Your voice sounded really off.

53:34.170 --> 53:36.119
I even canceled my PT session and came.

53:36.119 --> 53:38.666
I'm not okay.

53:38.666 --> 53:40.379
Two guys got into a fight because of me.

53:40.379 --> 53:42.362
It was a total mess.

53:42.362 --> 53:45.669
I was too scared.

53:45.669 --> 53:48.519
What did you even do on that blind date?

53:48.519 --> 53:50.949
You look really pale.

53:50.949 --> 53:52.263
I told you.

53:52.263 --> 53:53.960
When you rush into things, it backfires.

53:53.960 --> 53:55.571
Like after a hard workout...

53:55.571 --> 53:57.930
- You should rest...
- Seung Jun said

53:57.930 --> 54:00.377
after you push your body too hard,

54:00.377 --> 54:02.788
- you have to rest.
- You take a break before the next one.

54:02.788 --> 54:05.987
That's how you avoid getting hurt.

54:05.987 --> 54:08.465
- He said it's the same with your heart.
- Are you some kind of blind date pro?

54:08.465 --> 54:11.454
When I give you advice, at least listen.

54:21.627 --> 54:23.719
[Lee Hyun Ju]
[Are you still open to blind dates?]

54:27.105 --> 54:30.912
So I decided to take a break
from blind dates for a while.

54:30.912 --> 54:32.730
I wasn't giving up.

54:32.730 --> 54:34.763
It was more like crouching down

54:34.763 --> 54:37.496
to build momentum for later.

54:38.461 --> 54:40.269
Guys,

54:40.269 --> 54:41.809
let's call it a day.

54:41.809 --> 54:43.033
- Huh?
- Sorry?

54:43.033 --> 54:45.386
You've been covering my workload too.

54:45.386 --> 54:49.405
Today's on me. For everything!

54:50.076 --> 54:52.116
That's awkward.

55:00.220 --> 55:02.477
- Does it look okay?
- Yes.

55:02.477 --> 55:04.032
Sae Byeok!

55:04.032 --> 55:07.966
- Did it really not hurt?
- Not at all.

55:07.966 --> 55:09.496
Shouldn't you go first, Ui Yeong?

55:09.496 --> 55:10.844
You were worried about your dark spots.

55:10.844 --> 55:12.569
You know maintenance is everything, huh?

55:12.569 --> 55:14.473
This is super popular these days.

55:14.473 --> 55:16.715
I'm kind of scared though.

55:16.715 --> 55:17.760
Go on.

55:17.760 --> 55:20.488
Please take good care of her.

55:33.236 --> 55:36.076
It really doesn't hurt at all.

55:39.682 --> 55:41.172
Wait, wait!

55:41.172 --> 55:43.312
Hold on, hold on.

55:43.312 --> 55:46.032
That feels amazing.

55:47.692 --> 55:49.978
So nice.

55:51.025 --> 55:53.658
- Did you like it?
- Yes.

55:53.658 --> 55:57.038
Ui Yeong, you are the best.

55:59.350 --> 56:02.891
[Dad]

56:02.891 --> 56:05.296
[How have you been...]

56:05.296 --> 56:07.071
How have you been?

56:07.071 --> 56:08.569
I was working on something else recently,

56:08.569 --> 56:10.632
and you came to mind, so I'm reaching out.

56:10.632 --> 56:14.145
Stay healthy.

56:20.956 --> 56:23.175
But what needed to be set straight,

56:23.175 --> 56:25.749
had to be set straight.

56:26.362 --> 56:29.946
I definitely told him
you turned down the second date.

56:29.946 --> 56:34.559
So what, he just pretended not to know
and called you anyway?

56:34.559 --> 56:37.587
If you told him, that's enough.

56:37.587 --> 56:39.351
He's kind of weird.

56:39.351 --> 56:40.691
Are you okay?

56:40.691 --> 56:43.048
- You're not hurt, are you?
- No.

56:43.048 --> 56:44.418
He didn't shove me.

56:44.418 --> 56:46.016
He pushed one of the staff members.

56:46.016 --> 56:49.368
I was startled at the time, but I'm fine now.

56:49.368 --> 56:52.135
Hold on a second.

56:56.189 --> 56:59.325
Did you know about this or not?

56:59.325 --> 57:02.624
You two have been friends
for twenty years, right?

57:03.385 --> 57:07.536
Don't screw this up,
unless you want your engagement called off.

57:07.536 --> 57:10.783
Yeah, I just heard all this from Ui Yeong.

57:13.603 --> 57:16.546
[Tasting Event]
What are you talking about?

57:27.707 --> 57:29.815
Are you sure?

57:32.194 --> 57:33.880
Where are the parties involved right now?

57:33.880 --> 57:35.848
They're in the lobby.

57:35.848 --> 57:39.521
- Team Manager.
- Ms. Ui Yeong, just a moment.

57:40.881 --> 57:42.921
Ui Yeong!

57:42.921 --> 57:46.082
Have you seen this?

57:46.082 --> 57:47.292
[Pop-Up Exhibition at The Hills Seoul
Accused of Using Copycat Design]

57:47.292 --> 57:49.842
Copycat design?

57:55.425 --> 57:58.451
Someone needs to take responsibility
for what happened today.

57:58.451 --> 58:00.288
We sincerely apologize.

58:00.288 --> 58:02.055
I will make sure this is resolved.

58:02.055 --> 58:04.721
I'm very sorry.

58:11.108 --> 58:13.286
[Pop-Up Exhibition at The Hills Seoul
Accused of Using Copycat Design]

58:13.286 --> 58:14.803
[Is Its Credibility at Risk?]

58:14.803 --> 58:17.443
This is bold.

58:17.443 --> 58:19.313
And this was from last year?

58:19.313 --> 58:22.299
The tip came from the PR team at the museum
where the event was held.

58:22.299 --> 58:24.163
We've stated that we were unaware,

58:24.163 --> 58:26.989
but we can't say we're free of responsibility.

58:26.989 --> 58:29.667
It looks like there was already
a similar dispute before.

58:29.667 --> 58:32.265
Didn't the Purchasing Team vet the vendor?

58:32.265 --> 58:33.803
You didn't go ahead with it
knowing that, did you?

58:33.803 --> 58:36.266
What do you take us for?

58:36.266 --> 58:37.830
Of course not.

58:37.830 --> 58:40.868
Weren't we supposed to get a proposal
from another vendor as well?

58:40.868 --> 58:42.301
They had a strong portfolio.

58:42.301 --> 58:44.521
The vendor withdrew midway.

58:44.521 --> 58:46.358
It seemed like an internal issue,
so we didn't press further.

58:46.358 --> 58:48.158
We didn't drop them.

58:48.158 --> 58:51.788
Even if we take a loss,
we need to move forward with the event.

58:51.788 --> 58:52.985
If this ends like this,

58:52.985 --> 58:55.679
the hotel's reputation
could collapse overnight.

58:55.679 --> 58:58.688
If the brand raises an issue,
we'll have to compensate them anyway.

58:58.688 --> 59:01.451
We're better off taking control now
and resolving this ourselves.

59:01.451 --> 59:03.341
Then take responsibility and redo it.

59:03.341 --> 59:06.448
Sales and Marketing Team,
don't worry about the budget.

59:06.448 --> 59:07.559
- Got it.
- Purchasing Team,

59:07.559 --> 59:09.672
can you find another vendor
to handle the spatial design?

59:09.672 --> 59:10.825
We'll make it happen.

59:10.825 --> 59:12.127
Since the schedule's changed,

59:12.127 --> 59:15.968
we'll also reach back out to the vendors
that were planning to bid.

59:24.633 --> 59:26.155
Mrs. Na Ri...

59:26.155 --> 59:28.357
Hey.

59:28.357 --> 59:30.980
What is this? This is embarrassing.

59:30.980 --> 59:33.356
- You said you'd handle it yourself.
- Sorry.

59:33.356 --> 59:36.154
We'll take full responsibility.

59:50.952 --> 59:52.999
That startled you, right?

59:52.999 --> 59:55.162
Stuff like this happens
when you work long enough.

59:55.162 --> 59:57.077
I'll try to persuade them again.

59:57.077 --> 01:00:00.149
Send me the phone number of HOME's CEO.

01:00:00.149 --> 01:00:03.209
He's not going to take your call.

01:00:03.209 --> 01:00:05.967
Actually, they didn't cancel the meeting.

01:00:05.967 --> 01:00:08.076
What?

01:00:08.076 --> 01:00:11.283
I canceled it.

01:00:11.283 --> 01:00:12.646
What do you mean?

01:00:12.646 --> 01:00:14.346
Why would you do that?

01:00:14.346 --> 01:00:16.549
Mrs. Na Ri said...

01:00:16.549 --> 01:00:18.746
said we should just move forward with Homage.

01:00:18.746 --> 01:00:20.911
She said she'd take responsibility.

01:00:20.911 --> 01:00:24.574
So I thought I should wrap things up
on my end first...

01:00:24.574 --> 01:00:25.367
What?

01:00:25.367 --> 01:00:28.957
And Homage copied HOME's work.

01:00:29.651 --> 01:00:30.729
What?

01:00:30.729 --> 01:00:34.509
You gave me a chance and I blew it.
I'm so sorry.

01:00:38.663 --> 01:00:41.536
This is a complete mess.

01:00:48.958 --> 01:00:50.523
Hello?

01:00:50.523 --> 01:00:53.099
Is this CEO Lee Eun Ho?

01:00:53.099 --> 01:00:54.750
Yes, it is.

01:00:54.750 --> 01:00:58.513
Hi, this is Lee Ui Yeong
from The Hills Purchasing Team.

01:00:58.513 --> 01:01:00.657
I've been trying to reach you,

01:01:00.657 --> 01:01:03.253
but I couldn't get through.

01:01:03.253 --> 01:01:05.651
Oh, really?

01:01:05.651 --> 01:01:09.171
Well, if it's The Hills...

01:01:09.171 --> 01:01:11.301
I didn't take the calls on purpose.

01:01:11.301 --> 01:01:13.201
I saw the article.

01:01:13.201 --> 01:01:15.625
I was curious what kind of amazing proposal

01:01:15.625 --> 01:01:17.735
made you cancel our meeting.

01:01:17.735 --> 01:01:20.262
Turns out it was a direct copy of our work.

01:01:20.262 --> 01:01:22.166
You must've been very upset.

01:01:22.166 --> 01:01:25.199
I'd like to speak with you about that.

01:01:25.199 --> 01:01:27.324
Are you at the office right now?

01:01:27.324 --> 01:01:28.555
Even if you come, you won't see me.

01:01:28.555 --> 01:01:30.108
I'm heading out now.

01:01:30.108 --> 01:01:32.966
Then may I ask where you're headed?

01:01:32.966 --> 01:01:35.680
I can come to you.

01:01:35.680 --> 01:01:38.630
You're going to chase me down wherever I go?

01:01:38.630 --> 01:01:42.408
Fine. I'm heading to Chuncheon.
Why don't you try coming there?

01:01:42.408 --> 01:01:44.981
- Alright, let's go.
- Hello?

01:01:44.981 --> 01:01:47.074
Let's go.

01:02:16.992 --> 01:02:21.351
He's definitely still inside.
He answered the phone.

01:02:59.678 --> 01:03:02.629
Did he really just leave?

01:03:02.629 --> 01:03:06.589
I don't even know where he is.
I can't just track him down.

01:03:16.746 --> 01:03:19.920
[The Seagull]
[Invitation Exchange Voucher]

01:03:20.700 --> 01:03:23.410
This is for today, too?

01:03:36.107 --> 01:03:38.907
Yeah, thank you.

01:03:53.475 --> 01:03:57.859
Thank you to everyone for visiting
Meru Arts Center today.

01:03:57.859 --> 01:03:59.924
The performance will begin shortly.

01:03:59.924 --> 01:04:01.254
- Hey.
- Oh.

01:04:01.254 --> 01:04:03.541
You seem more nervous than usual today.

01:04:03.541 --> 01:04:05.331
- Waiting for someone?
- No.

01:04:05.331 --> 01:04:06.998
Just a friend.

01:04:06.998 --> 01:04:08.733
- A friend?
- Yeah.

01:04:08.733 --> 01:04:11.205
Food and beverages, including water,

01:04:11.205 --> 01:04:13.832
are not permitted inside the theater.

01:04:13.832 --> 01:04:16.692
For everyone's comfort,

01:04:16.692 --> 01:04:21.706
please turn off your cell phones
and all electronic devices.

01:04:21.706 --> 01:04:24.986
You're welcome to take photos
during the curtain call

01:04:24.986 --> 01:04:28.512
after the performance has ended.

01:04:34.580 --> 01:04:36.018
I really came

01:04:36.018 --> 01:04:38.604
all the way here.

01:04:38.604 --> 01:04:40.638
A mountain is a mountain,

01:04:40.638 --> 01:04:43.151
water is water,

01:04:43.151 --> 01:04:45.571
and I...

01:04:46.165 --> 01:04:48.944
I'm just the worker.

01:05:10.360 --> 01:05:11.820
Catch me if you can!

01:05:11.820 --> 01:05:14.076
- Be careful!
- No!

01:06:44.707 --> 01:06:47.453
Hello.

01:06:47.453 --> 01:06:51.826
I'm Lee Ui Yeong. I called earlier.

01:06:53.463 --> 01:06:55.850
Excuse me?

01:06:57.790 --> 01:07:00.443
Sir?

01:07:09.891 --> 01:07:12.252
Sir.

01:07:18.170 --> 01:07:20.590
Sir?

01:07:23.152 --> 01:07:24.316
Sir...

01:07:24.316 --> 01:07:26.422
Oh my!

01:07:26.422 --> 01:07:29.182
Oh my gosh, I'm so sorry.

01:07:31.276 --> 01:07:32.581
So sorry.

01:07:32.581 --> 01:07:35.034
My phone...

01:07:38.019 --> 01:07:40.186
Mr. Tae Seop?

01:07:40.186 --> 01:07:42.919
What are you doing here?

01:07:45.350 --> 01:07:46.884
Ms. Ui Yeong?

01:07:46.884 --> 01:07:48.421
Did you come to see me?

01:07:48.421 --> 01:07:50.294
What? Me?

01:07:50.294 --> 01:07:53.284
No, no. I'm here for work.

01:07:55.322 --> 01:07:58.048
Don't tell me... you're...

01:07:58.048 --> 01:08:00.765
- I'm the CEO of HOME.
- Oh, you are.

01:08:00.765 --> 01:08:03.062
So you're the CEO of HOME...

01:08:03.062 --> 01:08:05.091
What?

01:08:17.755 --> 01:08:21.624
[A one-percent chance?]
[An opportunity is still an opportunity.]

01:08:21.624 --> 01:08:24.921
[Today's to-do: Blind date]
[Tomorrow's to-do: Blind date]

01:08:24.921 --> 01:08:28.378
[I guess this is where our story ends.]

01:08:28.378 --> 01:08:32.151
[Ms. Ui Yeong]
[Ms. Seoltang]

01:08:35.272 --> 01:08:38.732
[I just didn't want to be
completely fake with you.]

01:08:45.227 --> 01:08:46.690
Why are you here?

01:08:46.690 --> 01:08:47.975
Oh, a shooting star!

01:08:47.975 --> 01:08:49.447
Hurry. Make a wish.

01:08:49.447 --> 01:08:53.449
If Ms. Ui Yeong's okay with it,
let's have her stay the night.

01:08:54.174 --> 01:08:57.128
I kept waiting, thinking maybe you'd show up.

01:08:57.128 --> 01:08:58.171
How about tomorrow night?

01:08:58.171 --> 01:09:00.803
- Ms. Ui Yeong.
- Oh...

01:09:00.803 --> 01:09:03.028
It's a basketball comic, so how about a game?

01:09:03.028 --> 01:09:05.489
If I win...

01:09:05.489 --> 01:09:07.972
You didn't come to apologize. So tell me.

01:09:07.972 --> 01:09:09.160
It's pouring outside!

01:09:09.160 --> 01:09:10.496
Ms. Ui Yeong!

01:09:10.496 --> 01:09:12.401
How do you want me

01:09:12.401 --> 01:09:15.600
to remember you?
